# Line endings the gate needs. sh cannot run a script with CRLF line endings, and Git for
# Windows' default core.autocrlf=true checks text files out with CRLF, so a clone there had
# a gate, hooks and doctor.sh that could not start. Every shell script and git hook checks out
# with LF on every platform, whatever a clone's autocrlf says (docs/DEV_SETUP.md, section 1).
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
